  "implemented": [
    "CPU source-picture prototype: competing native edge candidates, bounded sampled topology, glyph separation, exterior contradiction and independently supported canvas inference. Measured geometry remains distinct from discard permission; no standard-ratio snapping.",
    "Opt-in existing-worker shadow observation: defaults off, admission at most once per 500ms, 12ms cooperative deadline, source-owned results, no new queue or render-thread pixel scan.",
    "Separate foreground scan, original bounded background dispatch and ready-consumption permissions. Expired tickets and compatible backlog cannot hide exact ready evidence; no added dwell, repeat votes, expiry dispatch or relaxed source/context checks.",
    "Existing accepted-cue seed certificate now covers strong current three-line acquisition confirmed by four complete raw sources, despite pruned caller grouping. Current pixels, exact ownership, independent bars, age and nonrenewal checks remain required.",
    "Computed-only bounded pending-seed diagnostics and failure-tail records distinguish missing proof from current-pixel rejection or expiration.",
    "28 new required contracts plus 13 existing conversion/parity contracts added to the mandatory gate. Broader GPU wrapper can verify and reuse qualified binaries instead of rebuilding and deleting qualification."
  ],
